A||||2||Greg Piet||Is this a small Head gasket leak?||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||04-04-2001||05:18 PM||||I am NOT blowing smoke out of the exhaust pipes, but I have excessive smoke out of the PCV ports, and smoke coming out somewhere in the intake manifold area.  I cannot lock it down, but i think i is coming from some tube under the top manifold (likely somewhere from the PCV valve tube).  <P>It appears white (coolant), but does not have a typically sweet smell, and does not smell like gasoline vapors.  It is a fairly neutral smell (this coming from a smoker so it may actually be sweet and I cannot tell).  I tried to see if it was just the light that made the smoke appear white, so I put a drop or 2 of oil on the exhaust manifold, and that was definitely blue, while the smoke in question is white apparently.<P>I am not noticing a loss of coolant although it has only been about 30 miles of distance traveled.  The oil does not seem frothy, so I do not think there are large quantities of coolant getting into the oil.  <P>Typically the smoke is minimal at idle (not even observed a good amount of time, but when traveling down the road I see the smoke coming from my decklid vents.  It appears to be more pronounced under load (while in gear, thus higher rpm's than idle), and at higher speed.  The smoke is greater when I increase the rpm's with the decklid open but I am unsure if it is producing the same amount of smoke as when I am driving.  <P>My guess is that I need to re-do the head gaskets...  While I am attempting this what else could this be and what else should I be looking for.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 CSP<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">   <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cozmo||04-05-2001||08:05 AM||||I had similar symptoms and yes, in my case it was a blown head gasket.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009057.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009057.html</A> <BR>After tearing it down, I found the "smoking gun".<BR>Right by cyl. #5 lower left corner there was an obvious track between the cyl. and water jacket. <BR>Try some of the things I did, they can give you a lot of info about what may be wrong without tearing into it.<BR>BTW, I'm going to re-assemble it this weekend...after sacrificing a small animal to the Fiero Gods...<BR>(Fingers and other appendages crossed) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Good luck!!!<P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 2M6 Targa<BR>'86 GT<BR>'87 Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||04-05-2001||03:02 PM||||I saw a little green just under the valley cover...<P>I guess it is the head gasket, as the valley cover gaskets to the head were in good shape.<P>There  might have been a little visible seepage of AF from the block/head mating surface while the head was still attached...  Not sure if that is the culprit yet...<BR>I guess it is just put it back together and hope for the best.<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 04-06-2001).]||||reg||1
